# Copy to .env and edit, or just export these in your shell. .env is
# gitignored; this file is the committed template and must never contain a
# real value.

# --- Database. These are the defaults, so you can delete the lot if they fit.
WIKIRAG_HOST=127.0.0.1
WIKIRAG_PORT=3306
WIKIRAG_USER=root
WIKIRAG_PASSWORD=
WIKIRAG_DB=wikirag

# --- Embedding device. Auto-detects CUDA; set this to override.
# EMBED_DEVICE=cpu

# --- Answering model. OPTIONAL, AND DELIBERATELY SO.
#
# Every measured number in this repository is produced with `--no-llm` and no
# key at all (requirement A7): retrieval, recall, latency and hit@k are all
# reproducible without an account. Generation is the only step that needs a
# key, and without one `answer.py` prints the retrieved passages and says so
# rather than failing.
#
# Set ONE of these. Whichever you set, it is read from the environment and
# never written back to a file.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
#
# Override the answering model if you want a different one. The answering
# model need not match the embedding model and need not be either of these
# providers (08_rag_pipeline.md).
# ANSWER_MODEL=gemini-flash-latest
